# The exact smartmontools release RefurbMan bundles.
#
# Both vendor-smartmontools.sh and vendor-smartmontools.ps1 read this file, so
# the version and its checksums are stated once. Bump the version and the two
# hashes together; anything else is refused by the download step.
#
# Checksums are SHA-256, computed from downloads whose upstream-published MD5
# was verified first. Upstream signs releases with GPG and publishes MD5 only,
# so the SHA-256 values here were produced locally from verified bytes. Pinning
# them means the bundle cannot change underneath us even if the release files
# are replaced.
SMARTMONTOOLS_VERSION=7.5
# The mirror host directly. The project /download page is an interstitial
# that redirects twice, and a mirror answering it with an HTML page yields a
# checksum mismatch that reads like tampering when it is really a bad mirror.
SMARTMONTOOLS_BASE_URL=https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/smartmontools/smartmontools
SMARTMONTOOLS_SOURCE_SHA256=690b83ca331378da9ea0d9d61008c4b22dde391387b9bbad7f29387f2595f76e
SMARTMONTOOLS_WIN32_SHA256=896337fcc253220614cf8cdbd5cf2321c5aa326a37a04160a672a281e6104c70
